finding: The timed retry fixes loss at a stationary caller tick with a normally advancing clock, but the send-rate bound is not enforced when the caller's tick changes more than once per fixed step. IntentSender.record sets the flush default _tick even for operations (intent.ts:333–343), and flush treats every value different from the last as a fresh send slot (intent.ts:346,373–386). Operations can use different valid target ticks within one frame; alternating between two target ticks reopens a send on each record/flush pair without advancing transport time. The new test uses only one target tick for all 20 operations (upstream.test.ts:108–114), so it does not establish the stated bound for the public API.
